# Introductory Materials Laboratory.

**Authors:** Ritter, John E., Jr.

## Abstract
Described is an introductory materials science laboratory program which emphasizes crystal structure both on the atomistic and microscopic scale and the dependence of materials properties on structure. The content of this program is classified into four major areas: (1) materials science, (2) mechanical behavior of materials, (3) materials testing and evaluation, and (4) mechanical processing of materials. An introduction presenting the program objectives is also included. (HM)

**Source:** https://eric.ed.gov/?id=ED180753

